A generic anchor whose only result is a cleanup: Setup's type parameter appears
solely in its input's type argument (Box[T]) and nothing pins it, so T is lifted
onto the injector header while the anchor is instantiated unconditionally. The
demanded Box[T] is served by NewBox at the lifted T, and Setup's func() folds
into the aggregated cleanup.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Box[T any] struct{}

//plumb:build
func NewBox[T any]() Box[T] { return Box[T]{} }

//plumb:build
func Setup[T any](b Box[T]) func() { return func() {} }
